    JS disabled" rule. I won't fix it unless you want me to, but filters shouldn't make it worse.

  First question: which ways of narrowing should this cover?

  [1mThe fork:[0m how many filter dimensions we add. That sets the diff size (the 300-line limit) and how much guideline
  surface the reviewers check.

  - [1mEvent type only:[0m one Select with "All events" plus the nine types. This is the smallest diff and covers the
    failed-sign-in case ("Sign-in failed"). It can't narrow by date or device. Cheap to extend later.
  - [1mEvent type + date range:[0m adds two date pickers with presets. Per 03 Forms, a date range needs start/end validation,
    [38;5;153mdate_order[39m messages and presets, so it roughly doubles the guideline surface. Useful for "what happened last
    Tuesday", but with 90 days and around 300 rows at most, scrolling a type-filtered list already gets most of the way
    there.
  - [1mEvent type + text search over device/location:[0m adds a search field (type=search, clear button, Escape clears). It
    helps with "anything from Madrid?" or "Firefox on Windows", and pairs well with spotting unrecognized failed
    sign-ins.

  [1mMy recommendation:[0m event type only for this change, with a matching-row count announced politely (4.1.3). It answers
  the actual support-ticket question with the smallest review surface. Search or date range can follow as separate
  commits if they turn out to be needed.

